insert into documents (doc_type,title,source_url,doc_date,body) values ('news','Notice of Wastewater Effluent Hauling - August 2026','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/notice-of-wastewater-effluent-hauling-august-2026/','2026-08-10','Notice of Wastewater Effluent Hauling - August 2026 - Jul 31, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices Please be advised that commenc ing in ea rly August 2026, Wessuc Inc. will begin transporting wastewater effluent from the W astewater Facility 202 (Bayshore Village) to Wastewater Facility 201 (Lagoon City/Brechin) on behalf of the Township of Ramara (see map). While in effect, h auling will occur Monday to Friday between 6 a.m. and 6 p.m. While the new Tile Bed project is under construction, it was anticipated that favourable weather conditions and construction progress would allow the spray fields to maintain appropriate lagoon levels until such time as multiple cells in the tile bed are commissioned and available to receive effluent discharge. In 2025, lagoon levels were intentionally lowered in anticipation of construction in 2026 and 2027, as well as to manage winter operating conditions. However, the winter season brought significant snowfall, estimated at approximately 5 m, followed by an exceptionally wet spring. Localized flooding occurred throughout Ramara Township near Lake St. John, Lake Dalrymple, and Lake Simcoe. Precipitation has remained above average through the spring and summer, with more than 400 mm recorded between April 1 and July 30, 2026. The combination of above-average precipitation, higher-than-expected winter flows, and periods of high winds, which restrict operations under the facility''s Certificate of Approval, has necessitated the initiation of effluent hauling. Staff, Wessuc, and the Ontario Clean Water Agency (OCWA), as the Township’s Operating Authority, will continue to closely monitor lagoon levels and will limit hauling to the volume required to maintain regulatory compliance. Duivenvoorden Haulage Ltd. (DHL) and Tatham Engineering continue to advance the Tile Bed project, and progress updates are available on the Township’s website at ramara.ca/Project202 . Key Map Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','More vendors, more fun: Ramara Harvest Festival returns Aug. 29 | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/more-vendors-more-fun-ramara-harvest-festival-returns-aug-29/','2026-08-10','More vendors, more fun: Ramara Harvest Festival returns Aug. 29 By Township of Ramara - Aug 05, 2026 Media Releases Ramara, Ont. / Aug. 5, 2026 – The Township of Ramara''s Atherley Community Centre Board is excited to welcome residents and visitors back for the second annual Ramara Fall Harvest Festival on Saturday, Aug. 29, 2026, from 8 a.m. to 2 p.m. at Atherley Community Park on Creighton Street in Ramara (Atherley). Following the success of last year''s inaugural event, this year''s festival is returning with more than 30 local vendors, including local farmers, produce growers, artisans, makers and community organizations, offering an even wider variety of products, activities and experiences for the whole family while celebrating the harvest season. "We''re thrilled to see the Ramara Fall Harvest Festival return for a second year and continue to grow," said Mayor Basil Clarke. "This event showcases the incredible talent, creativity and community spirit that make Ramara such a special place. I encourage everyone to come out, support our local vendors and enjoy a great day with family, friends and neighbours." Visitors can browse handcrafted goods, jewelry, pottery, woodworking, dreamcatchers, baked goods, artisan creations, 3D printed products, and more while enjoying delicious food from local vendors. Community organizations, including Ramara Fire & Rescue Services, Simcoe County Paramedics with therapy dogs, and the Ontario Provincial Police will also be on site, making it a fun and welcoming event for all ages. The Ramara Fall Harvest Festival is free to attend and offers residents and visitors an opportunity to celebrate the harvest season while supporting local businesses, artisans and community organizations. "The response to our first Harvest Festival was incredible, and we''re excited to bring it back even bigger this year," said Steve Hinton, Chair of the Atherley Community Centre Board. "With more than 30 vendors and a great mix of local artisans, food, community partners and activities, farmers, there''s something for everyone. We look forward to welcoming the community for another fantastic day." Parking will be available along Creighton Street. The event will take place rain or shine. For more information about the event, please contact Patti from the Atherley Community Centre Board at 705-325-8900 (please leave a message). Residents browse local vendors and enjoy the Ramara Fall Harvest Festival during last year''s event at Atherley Community Park. The festival returns on Saturday, Aug. 29, 2026, with more than 30 vendors, local food, artisans and family-friendly activities. Left to Right: Sullivan and Winston Stong pose at the harvest-themed photo station overlooking Lake Simcoe at Atherley Community Park during last year''s Ramara Fall Harvest Festival. The festival returns on Saturday, Aug. 29, 2026, with more than 30 local vendors, artisan goods, fresh produce, food and family-friendly activities. Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!'),('news','Notice of Complete Application and Public Meeting - Zoning By-law Amendment (Z-2/26) | Township of Ramara','https://www.ramara.ca/news/posts/notice-of-complete-application-and-public-meeting-zoning-by-law-amendment-z-226/','2026-08-06','Notice of Complete Application and Public Meeting - Zoning By-law Amendment (Z-2/26) - Aug 06, 2026 Public Meetings and Notices Planning Notices Take Notice that the Council of The Corporation of the Township of Ramara deemed the following application a “Complete” application under Section 34 of the Planning Act on the July 31, 2026. And Take Notice that the Council of the Corporation of the Township of Ramara will hold a Public Meeting to consider the proposed Zoning By -law Amendment pursuant to Section 34 of the Planning Act , R.S.O. 1990, c.P.13, as amended Date and Time Meeting Location Monday, September 14, 2026 Commencing at 9:30 A.M. Council Chambers (2297 Highway 12, Brechin) and Zoom Platform File Number: Z-2/26 Subject Property: 2284 Concession Road 10 Legal Description: Concession 10, South Part Lot 11, Mara Owner: Michael and Yolanda Sternberg Agent: Ecovue Consulting Services Inc . (c/o Aditya Srinivas) Purpose and Effect: To prohibit residential uses and allow for a reduction in lot area and frontage for the land being retained as part of a consent application to sever a surplus farm dwelling. Proposed Lot Frontage: 52 metres Proposed Lot Area: 19 hectares (~ 47 acres) This amendment is a condition of consent to sever the surplus farm dwelling, which was approved by the Committee of Adjustment on February 10, 2026. (Consent File B-1/26) Information Available: Additional Information relating to the proposed amendments is available for inspection upon request at the Municipal Office by contacting the Planning Department between 9:00 a.m. and 4:30 p.m., (705) 484-5374 or by email to planning@ramara.ca . To view a copy of this notice and the draft amendments, visit www.ramara.ca/planningnotices Notification of Decision: If you wish to be notified of Council’s decision regarding the proposed Zoning By-law Amendment, you must submit a written request to the Municipal Clerk using one of the methods above prior to Council rendering a decision. Written Submission: Any person may make a written submission either in support of, or in opposition to, the proposed Zoning By-law Amendments. Signed written submissions will be accepted by the Municipal Clerk prior to the meeting. Submissions may be sent electronically to clerks@ramara.ca , faxed to (705) 484-0441, deposited in the mail drop box at the Township Administration Office or mailed. (Address provided at the end of this notice) Please ensure your name and address are included, as required for the public record. Oral and Written Submissions - Appeal: If a person or public body would otherwise have an ability to appeal the decision of the Council of the Township or Ramara to the Ontario Land Tribunal (OLT), but the person or public body does not make oral submissions at a public meeting or make written submissions to the Township of Ramara before the by -law is passed, the person or public body is not entitled to appeal the decision. If a person or public body does not make oral submissions at a public meeting, or make written submissions to the Township of Ramara before the by -law is passed, the person or public body may not be added as a party to the hearing of an appeal before the Ontario Land Tribunal (OLT) unless, in the opinion of the Tribunal, there are reasonable grounds to do so. Individuals who make written submissions should be aware that their submission and any personal information in their correspondence will become part of the public record and made available to the Applicant and Council. Learn More: For more information about this matter, including information about appeal rights, contact planning@ramara.ca Dated at the Township of Ramara this 6 th Day of August 2026. Clerks Department Planning Department P. 705-484-5374 ext. 261 E. ramara@ramara.ca P. 705-484-5374 ext. 251 E. planning@ramara.ca LOCATION MAP Notice of Complete Application And Public Meeting - Z-2/26 Draft Zoning By-law Amendment Subscribe Back to News Search Contact Us Corporation of the Township of Ramara 2297 Highway 12, PO Box 130, Brechin, ON, L0K 1B0 T. 705-484-5374 E. ramara@ramara.ca Sign up for our eNewsletter Stay up to date on the Township''s activities, events, programs and operations by subscribing to have notifications sent directly to your inbox. Sign Up Today!') on conflict (source_url) do nothing;